ng that has more  influence with him than his own will and  judgment this is a person who is  genuinely independent autonomous there  are not autonomous in the sense that  they can do anything whatsoever because  if they choose to do the wrong things  they're actually in a cert  sounds destroying that very you know  autonomy that they have that very  freedom that they have and what they're  doing is throwing it away in a certain  sense Cicero will go on and tell us that  the person who is wise in this way the  beautiful phrase does nothing against  his will why because he is restricting  his will to what he can actually  accomplish he does nothing by compulsion  and as Cicero will say he does nothing  in regret it's totally the opposite for  the person who is foolish and one of the  things that is most characteristic of  foolish people tends to be the fact that  they don't actually realize that they  are foolish and Cicero says that by  being foolish they are actually placing  themselves in the the category of being  slaves they are enslaving themselves  they are using the freedom that they  have in the wrong way and thereby  essentially nullifying that freedom so  he goes on and he says you know some  examples that he has are all wicked men  are slaves he says nor is this so  startling a thing as as it sounds we  don't mean that they're slaves in the  sense of chattels that they've become  the property of their Lords for debt or  some law of state but if slavery means  as it does mean he says the obedience of  a broken and abject spirit that has no  volition of its own that can't actually  decide for itself no judgment of its own  no our bit reom right who would deny  that all light-minded and covetous  people and indeed all the vicious people  are really slaves those who are covetous  those who desire all sorts of things  like money or you know fancy houses or  you know decked out cars or having the  best stereo system in the world I don't  know if people do that 